rce/sestatus show Enforcing before, during, and after the fix and restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof SELinux was actually the enforcing control (not bypassed) for the non-standard port\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ff2fbe8d7e1e49e2\",\"cmd-46ce7bc64d2c4234\",\"cmd-fb0d8881ac714a30\"],\"summary\":\"httpd failed to bind 8181 with Permission denied while 8181 was absent from http_port_t; after semanage port -a adding 8181 to http_port_t, bind succeeded\"},{\"requirement\":\"External reachability (firewall) for the service\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8d3d3470b3cc45ec\",\"cmd-b992becf2b504fd3\",\"cmd-6d97886edbf54b82\"],\"summary\":\"firewalld initially lacked port 8181; opened and reloaded permanently; confirmed present after reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1f96fef75fcf47b5\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 71f12f87-337d-4ff3-b414-9680244c2694, SELinux Enforcing, httpd active, curl HTTP 200\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3a69aec2d28e4a3d\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded systemctl reboot returned 'reboot-scheduled' acknowledgement immediately\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart actually occurred (changed boot identity) and node became reachable again\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bd6f4cd6a3124688\",\"cmd-eb7c0f6543304888\",\"cmd-73f3b867f6cb4a28\",\"cmd-d7f83cbaab8b46f4\",\"cmd-860542d595fa4b59\",\"cmd-ec90603879f049dd\"],\"summary\":\"Node connection dropped/timed out across several polls, then exec succeeded again; new boot_id 383d9e44-a321-4a71-8a48-9acab6a5754f differs from baseline, proving an actual reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of required services/data and SELinux state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ec90603879f049dd\",\"cmd-6d97886edbf54b82\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot: SELinux Enforcing, httpd active+enabled, listening on 8181, SELinux port context and firewalld rule persisted, curl returns HTTP 200 with correct in